exav-imagehash: third-party notices
===================================

exav-imagehash is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). Parts of its
source are derived from other projects; this file gives their notices, and
each directory's README says what was changed. The notices for the components
the exav binaries link are in the NOTICE file at the root of the exav
repository: https://github.com/sylvinus/exav/blob/main/NOTICE


The JPEG and TIFF decoders this crate hashes through (adapted from image
0.25.9 and tiff 0.10.3) are in exav-render's `src/image_codecs/`, with their
licenses and notices.


rustdct, MIT OR Apache-2.0 (source derivative)
----------------------------------------------

src/dct.rs holds rustdct 0.7.1's DCT-II for power-of-two lengths, with bounds
checks where upstream skips them with `unsafe`. Used under the MIT License,
whose text is in src/LICENSE-rustdct.

Upstream: https://github.com/ejmahler/rust_dct
